# Skills are authored in rocket-agents, nowhere else

Unscoped on purpose: the moment this matters is the first `Write` of a new
`SKILL.md`, before any skill file has been read and before any path-scoped rule
can fire. The superpowers `writing-skills` skill says personal skills live in
`~/.claude/skills/`. On this estate that advice deletes the skill.

**The only source is `~/p/rocket-agents/src/skills/core/<name>/SKILL.md`**,
registered by name in `src/skills/skill-rules.map.json`. Everything else is
generated output that `pnpm run skills:link` wipes and rewrites from `dist/`:
`~/.claude/skills/<name>` is a symlink into `~/.agents/skills/core/`, which is
the `rocket-agents-library` checkout, and `compileLibraryTarget` removes that
whole tree before repopulating it. A skill written into the library, into
`~/.claude/skills/` or into a project's `.claude/skills/` survives until the next
link and no longer. On 2026-09-11 `ui-verification-loop` was authored in the
library, committed there three times, and erased that night; it was rebuilt
from the library's history on 2026-09-12 and moved into source.

Ship sequence, gates, the self-healing section and the `Trigger when` /
`Do not use` requirements are in `skill-self-healing` (loaded when a
`SKILL.md` is in scope). What must be known before that rule loads is only the
location: source in rocket-agents, map entry, `skills:compile`, `skills:link`.
